# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env` for local development.
#
# Everything here is compiled into the bundle by Vite and is therefore public —
# never put a secret in a VITE_ variable. `.env` is gitignored all the same,
# because what it decides is which backend every build talks to, and a
# committed value quietly wins over whatever the deployment meant to use.
#
# The public production API URL is set in the Static Web Apps GitHub Actions
# workflow. Change that value when the backend moves to a custom domain.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The backend origin, with no trailing slash. Must be https in production:
# a page served over https cannot call an http API, and the browser blocks it
# as mixed content with no visible error beyond a console line.
#
# This is also the Better Auth server the client talks to (it calls
# <VITE_SERVER_URL>/api/auth/*), so the same origin covers both.
VITE_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000
